♪ I never can
 say goodbye, girl ♪

14:28.402 --> 14:30.234
♪ Oh, no, no ♪

14:30.369 --> 14:32.239
-♪ Hey, baby ♪
-♪ Never can say goodbye ♪

14:32.375 --> 14:35.078
(audience chatters excitedly)

14:35.214 --> 14:36.574
♪ No, no, no, no, no, no... ♪

14:36.709 --> 14:38.918
I'll be in touch, Mr. Jackson.

14:39.054 --> 14:41.882
♪ I never can say
goodbye, girl ♪

14:42.017 --> 14:44.917
JERMAINE: ♪ I'm never gonna
say goodbye, baby ♪

14:45.053 --> 14:47.225
MICHAEL: ♪ I never can say
goodbye, girl, yeah ♪

14:47.360 --> 14:49.290
JERMAINE:
♪ I'm never gonna say ♪

14:49.425 --> 14:52.066
♪ No, no, no, no, no, no ♪

14:52.835 --> 14:55.197
♪ No, no, no, no, no, no. ♪

14:55.333 --> 14:57.095
-(song ends)
-(cheering and applause)

14:57.231 --> 14:58.566
("Money (That's What I Want)"
by Barrett Strong playing)

14:58.701 --> 15:00.304
♪ The best things in life
are free ♪

15:00.440 --> 15:03.036
♪ But you can give them
to the birds and bees ♪

15:03.171 --> 15:06.313
-♪ I need money ♪
-♪ That's what I want ♪

15:06.448 --> 15:08.775
-♪ That's what I want ♪
-♪ That's... ♪

15:08.911 --> 15:10.380
-JOSEPH: All right, boys,
look alive.
-Hi, Mr. Gordy.

15:10.516 --> 15:11.784
-JOSEPH: Mr. Gordy's here.
-GORDY: Suzanne.

15:11.919 --> 15:13.417
Boys, good to see you again.

15:13.552 --> 15:15.255
Y'all been learning
the song we gave you?

15:15.391 --> 15:17.048
-Practicing night and day.
-We'll start with Michael.

15:17.184 --> 15:19.450
-("I Want You Back" playing)
-MICHAEL: ♪ Uh-huh ♪

15:19.586 --> 15:21.187
♪ Let me tell you now ♪

15:21.322 --> 15:24.163
♪ Uh-huh ♪

15:25.428 --> 15:27.365
♪ When I had you to myself ♪

15:27.501 --> 15:29.498
-♪ I didn't want you around ♪
-(music stops)

15:30.399 --> 15:32.298
GORDY:
Michael, um,

15:32.434 --> 15:34.303
you're moving too much.

15:34.439 --> 15:36.802
(over speaker):
All right, here we go.

15:37.471 --> 15:40.146
(music resumes playing)

15:41.907 --> 15:44.216
(music playing
through headphones)

15:49.221 --> 15:53.790
♪ Uh-huh, huh, huh, huh ♪

15:53.926 --> 15:55.187
(music stops)

15:56.290 --> 15:59.065
-(clicks button)
-Uh, Michael,
you're doing it again.

15:59.200 --> 16:01.193
Take a step closer
to the microphone.

16:01.329 --> 16:04.164
That's it. And I'm gonna need
you to keep your feet still.

16:04.299 --> 16:05.804
You understand me?

16:05.940 --> 16:08.233
Give me the same lead-up.

16:08.368 --> 16:10.138
(whirring)

16:10.273 --> 16:11.501
GORDY:
Here we go.

16:11.637 --> 16:14.642
(music resumes playing)

16:21.022 --> 16:24.724
♪ Uh-huh, huh, huh, huh ♪

16:24.860 --> 16:27.055
♪ Let me tell you now ♪

16:27.190 --> 16:29.360
♪ Huh, huh ♪

16:30.962 --> 16:36.026
♪ When I had you to myself
I didn't want you around ♪

16:36.162 --> 16:38.261
♪ Those pretty faces
always made you ♪

16:38.397 --> 16:40.098
-Let me talk to him.
-♪ Stand out in a crowd... ♪

16:40.234 --> 16:41.633
-No, he's just getting it.
-I just need five minutes.

16:41.769 --> 16:43.671
Say, Joseph,
why don't you worry

16:43.806 --> 16:45.569
about keeping the boys
on schedule, huh?

16:45.704 --> 16:47.541
We got this over here.

16:47.676 --> 16:50.579
♪ For me
to take a second look ♪

16:50.714 --> 16:53.580
♪ Oh, baby,
give me one more chance ♪

16:53.716 --> 16:55.455
♪ To show you that I love you ♪

16:55.590 --> 17:00.487
♪ Won't you please
let me back in your heart? ♪

17:00.622 --> 17:02.193
♪ Oh, darling, I was blind... ♪

17:02.329 --> 17:05.089
-What did I tell you?
-(laughs)

17:05.224 --> 17:09.536
♪ But now, since I see you
in his arms... ♪

17:09.671 --> 17:12.539
♪ When ♪

17:12.674 --> 17:15.774
♪ I ♪

17:15.909 --> 17:19.439
♪ Had you ♪

17:19.574 --> 17:26.083
♪ I treated you bad ♪

17:26.218 --> 17:29.052
♪ And wrong, my dear ♪

17:29.188 --> 17:31.725
♪ And, girl, since ♪

17:31.861 --> 17:37.030
♪ Since you went away ♪

17:37.165 --> 17:41.792
♪ Don't you know I sit around ♪

17:41.928 --> 17:46.167
♪ With my head hanging down ♪

17:46.302 --> 17:49.074
♪ And I wonder ♪

17:49.209 --> 17:52.643
♪ Who's loving you ♪

17:53.413 --> 17:58.679
(fading):
♪ I, I, I, I... ♪

17:58.815 --> 18:00.978
GORDY:
 Let me tell you something, son.

18:01.113 --> 18:03.788
I've been doing this
a long time.

18:04.524 --> 18:06.452
I've never heard a voice
quite like yours.

18:07.055 --> 18:09.990
You sang that song
better than Smokey himself.

18:10.126 --> 18:11.858
Really?

18:13.395 --> 18:14.993
You're special.

18:15.828 --> 18:17.766
You have something to say.

18:18.402 --> 18:20.068
That's rare, Michael.

18:20.904 --> 18:22.833
GORDY: Yeah, this is
the fader. Come on, try it.

18:22.968 --> 18:25.407
Here, this fader
goes up and down

18:25.542 --> 18:26.972
-and it sets the levels
-Wow.

18:27.107 --> 18:28.678
-to the volume.
-("I Want You Back" playing)

18:28.814 --> 18:30.885
It can make your voice
sound... (loudly): louder...

18:31.020 --> 18:32.379
(softly):
...or softer.

18:32.514 --> 18:33.979
-All right?
-Yeah.

18:34.115 --> 18:36.019
And these knobs up here,
that's for your EQ.

18:36.154 --> 18:37.316
What's EQ?

18:37.452 --> 18:39.187
Equalization.

18:39.323 --> 18:40.523
You see, when we record,

18:40.658 --> 18:42.053
we split things up
in tracks, right?

18:42.188 --> 18:43.458
JOSEPH: Excuse me, uh,
time to go, Michael.

18:43.593 --> 18:45.222
Mr. Gordy's a very busy man.

18:45.358 --> 18:46.699
I'm sure you've taken up
enough of his time.

18:46.834 --> 18:48.834
(chuckles)

18:48.969 --> 18:50.667
MICHAEL (recording): ♪ Back in
your heart? Oh, darlin'... ♪

18:50.802 --> 18:52.596
Go ahead on, Michael.
I can show you this stuff

18:52.732 --> 18:54.264
some other time, right?

18:54.399 --> 18:56.871
-Okay, Mr. Gordy. Thank you.
-All right. Mm-hmm.

18:57.006 --> 19:00.412
MICHAEL (recording):
♪ In his arms, uh-huh ♪

19:06.822 --> 19:08.217
Hey, Michael.

19:08.353 --> 19:10.482
You can ask me anything...

19:10.617 --> 19:12.191
anytime you want.

19:12.327 --> 19:14.518
(vocalizing)
♪ All I want ♪

19:14.653 --> 19:16.357
(vocalizing)

19:16.493 --> 19:18.822
♪ All I need... ♪

19:18.957 --> 19:21.235
("ABC" by Jackson 5 playing)

19:24.202 --> 19:26.201
♪ A, B, C ♪

19:26.336 --> 19:28.135
-♪ Easy as one, two, three ♪
-♪ One, two, three ♪

19:28.271 --> 19:29.900
-♪ Or simple as do-re-mi ♪
-♪ Do-re-mi ♪

19:30.035 --> 19:32.513
♪ A, B, C, one, two, three ♪

19:32.648 --> 19:34.678
-♪ Baby, you and me, girl ♪
-♪ You and me ♪

19:34.813 --> 19:36.883
-♪ A, B, C ♪
-♪ Easy as ♪

19:37.019 --> 19:38.816
♪ One, two, three ♪

19:38.952 --> 19:40.581
-♪ Or simple as do-re-mi ♪
-♪ Do-re-mi ♪

19:40.716 --> 19:42.886
♪ A, B, C, one, two, three ♪

19:43.021 --> 19:44.888
-♪ Baby, you and me, girl ♪
-♪ You and me ♪

19:45.024 --> 19:46.124
♪ Come on, let me love you
 just a little bit... ♪

19:46.259 --> 19:48.385
All right, so, how old are you?

19:48.521 --> 19:49.923
Ten.

19:50.058 --> 19:51.196
No, you're not ten.
You're eight.

19:51.332 --> 19:52.762
♪ Come on, come on, come on ♪

19:52.897 --> 19:54.400
♪ Let me show you
what it's all about ♪

19:54.535 --> 19:56.228
♪ Reading, writing,
'rithmetic... ♪

19:56.364 --> 19:58.530
In this business, you can
make up just about anything,

19:58.666 --> 19:59.932
especially your age.

20:00.067 --> 20:01.473
♪ Your education
ain't complete ♪

20:01.608 --> 20:02.900
♪ T-T-T,
teacher's gonna show you ♪

20:03.035 --> 20:04.208
♪ Show you, show you ♪

20:04.343 --> 20:06.074
♪ How to get an "A" ♪

20:06.209 --> 20:07.773
-♪ How to get an "A" ♪
-(reporters clamoring)

20:07.908 --> 20:09.881
♪ You add the two ♪

20:10.016 --> 20:11.684
JERMAINE: ♪ Listen to me, baby,
that's all you got to do ♪

20:11.819 --> 20:13.051
-MICHAEL: ♪ Oh, A, B, C ♪
-♪ A, B, C ♪

20:13.186 --> 20:14.882
♪ It's easy as ♪

20:15.017 --> 20:16.089
-♪ One, two, three ♪
-(clamoring)

20:16.224 --> 20:18.421
♪ Or simple as do-re-mi ♪

20:18.556 --> 20:20.793
♪ A, B, C, one, two, three ♪

20:20.929 --> 20:22.791
-♪ Baby, you and me, girl ♪
-♪ You and me... ♪

20:22.926 --> 20:25.096
-(reporters clamoring)
-REPORTER: Michael.

20:25.232 --> 20:27.128
Michael. How old are you?

20:27.263 --> 20:29.136
-♪ Sing a simple melody ♪
-♪ Do-re-mi ♪

20:29.271 --> 20:30.927
♪ A, B, C, that's how easy... ♪

20:31.063 --> 20:32.971
I'm, uh, I'm eight, sir.

20:33.107 --> 20:35.271
-(reporters clamoring)
-♪ That's how easy
love can be ♪

20:35.407 --> 20:37.403
-♪ Sing a simple melody ♪
-♪ That's how easy
love can be ♪

20:37.538 --> 20:38.903
(cheering)

20:39.039 --> 20:41.245
MICHAEL:
♪ Sit down, girl ♪

20:41.380 --> 20:44.049
♪ I think I love ya ♪

20:44.185 --> 20:46.482
♪ No, get up, girl ♪

20:46.617 --> 20:48.319
♪ Show me what you can do ♪

20:48.454 --> 20:49.984
♪ Shake it, shake it, baby ♪

20:50.119 --> 20:53.624
♪ Come on now,
shake it, shake it, baby ♪

20:54.720 --> 20:56.257
♪ Huh ♪

20:56.392 --> 20:57.592
♪ ♪

20:57.727 --> 21:00.058
♪ Ooh-ooh, A, B, C, baby ♪

21:00.194 --> 21:03.462
♪ Nah, nah, do-re-mi,
baby, ow! ♪

21:03.598 --> 21:05.606
(music fades)

21:05.741 --> 21:08.133
-(boys laughing, chattering)
-(peacock cawing in distance)

21:11.307 --> 21:14.074
MICHAEL: And I've been reading
about the Serengeti.

21:14.209 --> 21:18.951
Learning about all different
types of lions, tigers,

21:19.086 --> 21:21.484
monkeys, giraffes.

21:22.120 --> 21:25.453
One day, you and I will have
more friends to play with.

21:25.589 --> 21:27.020
Wouldn't that be fun?

21:28.122 --> 21:30.430
Look at this picture.
You like it?

21:31.262 --> 21:32.827
(rat squeaking)

21:32.962 --> 21:34.900
Come on, Michael,
Joseph wants you.

21:35.035 --> 21:36.702
(rat squeaking)

21:36.837 --> 21:39.796
And make sure you put your rat
in the cage this time.

21:39.931 --> 21:42.035
It's disgusting.

21:42.834 --> 21:45.471
Come on now.

21:45.606 --> 21:47.506
(clock chiming)

21:47.641 --> 21:49.142
Meet Bill Bray.

21:49.277 --> 21:51.151
He's your new
head of security, all right?

21:51.287 --> 21:52.644
Now, he's gonna
be around a lot.

21:52.780 --> 21:54.982
Make sure you mind him.

21:56.785 --> 21:58.315
Nice to meet you, Mr. Bray.

21:58.451 --> 22:00.357
It's very nice to meet you,
too, young man.

22:00.492 --> 22:01.828
You can call me Bill, okay?

22:01.963 --> 22:03.731
Okay, Bill.

22:03.866 --> 22:05.927
All right.

22:07.660 --> 22:10.234
-Guard him with your life.
-("Singin'
in the Rain" playing)

22:10.369 --> 22:11.664
(tap dancing over TV)

22:11.799 --> 22:12.865
KATHERINE:
Michael.

22:13.000 --> 22:14.640
You're missing the best part.

22:14.775 --> 22:17.136
("Singin' in the Rain"
continues over TV)

22:28.055 --> 22:30.391
♪ ♪

22:39.061 --> 22:40.727
MICHAEL:
And llamas have three stomachs,

22:40.863 --> 22:42.093
so they can digest their food

22:42.229 --> 22:44.331
because all they eat
is vegetables.

22:44.466 --> 22:46.837
And they're really smart,
very intelligent creatures.

22:46.972 --> 22:49.574
-And best of all,
they never ever bite.
-(chuckles)

22:49.710 --> 22:51.639
That's what you said
about the rats.

22:51.775 --> 22:53.612
No, really. Llamas never bite.

22:53.747 --> 22:56.107
They only spit
when they're agitated.

22:56.243 --> 22:58.078
So, you want me to bring
some spitting,

22:58.213 --> 23:00.047
-agitated animal into my house?
-(chuckles)

23:00.182 --> 23:02.187
He'll live outside.
Come on, please.

23:02.323 --> 23:03.855
-Please say yes.
-No.

23:03.990 --> 23:05.919
-I'll look after him.
-Absolutely not, Michael.

23:06.055 --> 23:08.723
Mother has enough things
to worry about.

23:08.858 --> 23:10.228
And you don't need another pet.

23:10.364 --> 23:11.823
They're not my pets.

23:11.959 --> 23:13.830
They're my friends.

23:14.763 --> 23:16.969
(Katherine inhales)

23:17.104 --> 23:19.231
Well... (sighs)

23:22.001 --> 23:24.236
I do understand that.

23:24.372 --> 23:26.012
But don't you want
to meet real friends,

23:26.148 --> 23:28.939
like, kids your own age?

23:29.075 --> 23:31.980
I would like that for you.

23:33.348 --> 23:37.051
I do sometimes,
but I'm not
like the other kids.

23:37.187 --> 23:39.985
They don't treat me
like a real person.

23:40.120 --> 23:42.325
And all they want
to do is stare

23:42.461 --> 23:44.322
and take pictures of me.

23:51.734 --> 23:54.332
You look at me, Michael.

23:55.767 --> 23:58.769
I knew you were different
the moment you were born.

23:59.605 --> 24:02.081
I knew you were different
from your brothers,

24:02.216 --> 24:04.349
and that's okay.

24:04.485 --> 24:07.411
You have a very special light.

24:08.213 --> 24:10.315
And you know what Jehovah says.

24:10.450 --> 24:14.722
He says, "Let your light shine
unto the world."

24:14.858 --> 24:18.329
Now, you let your light shine.

24:18.464 --> 24:21.095
Do you understand me?

24:22.630 --> 24:24.133
Yeah.

24:24.269 --> 24:27.574
Don't you ever let anyone
take that away from you.

24:28.638 --> 24:30.808
Not even yourself.

24:33.411 --> 24:34.713
Come here.

24:34.848 --> 24:36.880
("I'll Be There"
by Jackson 5 playing)

24:38.654 --> 24:40.314
(people chattering,
screaming happily)

24:40.450 --> 24:42.345
MICHAEL (over speakers):
The next song we're gonna do

24:42.481 --> 24:45.157
is one of our favorites.
You guys ready?

24:45.293 --> 24:47.818
(cheering, whooping)

24:47.953 --> 24:50.223
♪ ♪

24:52.028 --> 24:57.999
♪ You and I must make a pact ♪

24:58.135 --> 25:04.039
♪ We must
bring salvation back ♪

25:05.105 --> 25:08.641
♪ Where there is love ♪

25:08.777 --> 25:12.745
-♪ I'll be there ♪
-♪ I'll be there ♪

25:12.880 --> 25:14.918
♪ Oh, oh, yeah ♪

25:16.350 --> 25:20.424
♪ I'll be there
to protect you ♪

25:20.560 --> 25:21.724
♪ Yeah, baby ♪

25:21.859 --> 25:24.092
♪ With an unselfish love ♪

25:24.227 --> 25:26.723
-♪ That respects you ♪
-(cheering)

25:26.859 --> 25:27.894
Michael!

25:28.029 --> 25:32.229
♪ Just call my name ♪

25:32.364 --> 25:35.235
♪ And I'll be there ♪

25:35.969 --> 25:39.073
♪ And, oh ♪

25:39.208 --> 25:43.046
♪ I'll be there
to comfort you ♪

25:43.181 --> 25:46.247
♪ Build my world of dreams
around you ♪

25:46.382 --> 25:50.483
♪ I'm so glad
that I found you, baby ♪

25:50.619 --> 25:54.394
♪ I'll be there
with a love that's strong ♪

25:54.530 --> 25:56.797
♪ I'll be your strength ♪

25:57.533 --> 26:00.660
♪ I'll keep holding on ♪

26:00.795 --> 26:02.493
♪ Ooh ♪

26:06.239 --> 26:09.740
-♪ Yes, I will ♪
-♪ If you should ever find ♪

26:09.876 --> 26:13.207
-♪ Someone new ♪
-(cheering)

26:13.342 --> 26:18.850
♪ I know he better be
good to you ♪

26:20.282 --> 26:23.914
♪ 'Cause if he doesn't then ♪

26:24.050 --> 26:27.386
-♪ I'll be there ♪
-♪ I'll be there ♪

26:27.522 --> 26:31.826
♪ Don't you know, baby,
yeah, yeah ♪

26:31.961 --> 26:36.032
♪ I'll be there ♪

26:37.696 --> 26:41.965
(fading):
♪ I'll be there... ♪

26:42.101 --> 26:44.304
(music fades)

26:47.640 --> 26:51.480
MAN: Shedding the past,
embracing freedom...

26:52.316 --> 26:54.754
That's your album
right there, brother.

26:58.286 --> 27:00.155
MAN:
That's what people want.

27:01.187 --> 27:03.054
Pure escapism, Quincy.

27:03.190 --> 27:04.995
-That's it.
-Yeah.

27:07.960 --> 27:09.760
So...

27:09.896 --> 27:13.630
how are you gonna tell your
father about a solo album?

27:16.138 --> 27:18.169
Breaking away
from the family...

27:18.305 --> 27:20.637
he's not gonna like that.

27:23.376 --> 27:25.378
I'm not a kid anymore, Q.

27:27.284 --> 27:29.217
I'm gonna look him
straight in the eye.

27:30.689 --> 27:32.891
Tell him to his face.

27:34.121 --> 27:36.587
(breathing shakily)

27:39.066 --> 27:42.894
I need you to tell my father
that the solo album

27:43.030 --> 27:45.805
was your idea.

27:51.839 --> 27:53.241
Okay.

27:53.907 --> 27:55.881
Okay.

27:56.716 --> 27:58.345
I'm gonna have a drink.

27:58.480 --> 28:02.252
Michael, we love you
doing a solo album.

28:02.387 --> 28:05.023
Honestly, that's why
we signed you all to Epic.

28:05.158 --> 28:07.418
No disrespect to your family,
but... (chuckles)

28:07.554 --> 28:09.593
...this is what
we were hoping for.

28:09.729 --> 28:12.162
MICHAEL:
Great. I just...

28:12.297 --> 28:14.195
I think it'll be better
coming from you guys.

28:14.330 --> 28:16.161
Anything we can do
to help, Michael.

28:16.296 --> 28:18.928
So, tell us about the album.

28:19.064 --> 28:22.966
Okay. Well, this album,
it's really important to me.

28:23.101 --> 28:26.104
I just... I need the freedom
to write the music and lyrics

28:26.239 --> 28:28.672
that pop into my head.

28:28.807 --> 28:30.882
You know,
to express myself creatively.

28:31.018 --> 28:33.616
I want a whole new sound,
a whole new me.

28:33.752 --> 28:36.285
Quincy Jones producing.

28:36.420 --> 28:38.990
Rod Temperton,
he's working
on songs right now.

28:40.126 --> 28:42.889
(chuckles):
It sounds terrific, Michael.

28:43.024 --> 28:44.697
Consider it done.

28:44.833 --> 28:46.594
-(birds chirping)
-(water flowing)

28:46.730 --> 28:48.627
EXECUTIVE: So, we feel like
 Michael doing a solo album

28:48.762 --> 28:51.266
 would be really great
 for the label and,

28:51.401 --> 28:55.305
more importantly,
for the Jackson brand.

28:55.440 --> 28:57.268
They could help each other
with PR and merchandising

28:57.404 --> 29:00.873
and feed each other, you know?

29:01.009 --> 29:04.048
"Feed." Sure.

29:07.384 --> 29:11.616
So, I guess
you're okay with all this.

29:12.417 --> 29:13.883
Of course, gentlemen.

29:14.018 --> 29:16.929
Whatever's good for Michael
is great for me.

29:19.058 --> 29:20.895
And if there's anything
you need, don't hesitate to--

29:21.031 --> 29:22.968
JOSEPH:
Only thing is...

29:24.468 --> 29:26.797
Michael can do whatever
he wants in his spare time,

29:26.932 --> 29:29.843
so long as he continues
to work with his brothers.

29:32.239 --> 29:33.646
His... I'm sorry?

29:33.781 --> 29:36.308
I own his ass
from 9:00 to 5:00.

29:36.443 --> 29:38.184
After that, it's up to him.

29:38.319 --> 29:42.286
If he wants to cut an album
at midnight, so fine with me.

29:42.422 --> 29:45.983
As long as he's at that
microphone at 9:00 a.m. sharp.

29:46.919 --> 29:49.526
That's what works around here.
My house.

29:49.661 --> 29:51.656
