36:07.503 --> 36:09.874
(whispers):
Oh, wow.

36:10.010 --> 36:11.505
(chimp hoots softly)

36:11.640 --> 36:12.877
-(chuckles)
-HANDLER: Go on.

36:13.012 --> 36:14.172
It's okay.

36:14.308 --> 36:17.547
(hoots)

36:19.151 --> 36:21.048
(hoots inquisitively)

36:21.183 --> 36:22.249
Go on.

36:22.385 --> 36:24.422
No, it's okay.

36:27.653 --> 36:29.592
(chimp grunts)

36:34.765 --> 36:37.569
I want you to meet
my new friend, Bubbles.

36:37.705 --> 36:39.503
Oh.

36:39.639 --> 36:41.406
MICHAEL: I rescued him
from this awful place.

36:41.541 --> 36:44.109
You know, where they do
testing on animals.

36:44.244 --> 36:46.610
Welcome to the family.
(scoffs)

36:46.745 --> 36:50.008
Michael, you do know
that chimps are wild animals

36:50.144 --> 36:53.616
that don't belong
in a house in Encino.

36:53.751 --> 36:55.953
Mother, I'll take
good care of him.

36:56.088 --> 36:57.283
I will, I promise.

36:57.419 --> 36:59.155
Does he bite?

36:59.291 --> 37:01.758
Oh, no. No, he's sweet.

37:02.528 --> 37:04.393
-But, you know, chimps...
-(hoots)

37:04.528 --> 37:05.659
are sensitive,
though, you know,

37:05.794 --> 37:08.058
to certain sounds
and-and people.

37:08.194 --> 37:11.634
You know, they either hide
or they attack.

37:13.533 --> 37:15.572
(chuckles)

37:17.878 --> 37:19.438
♪ ♪

37:19.573 --> 37:21.413
(Bubbles huffing)

37:21.549 --> 37:23.948
MICHAEL:
It's okay, Bubbles. It's okay.

37:24.083 --> 37:26.011
You're safe now.

37:27.252 --> 37:28.516
(tambourine rattles)

37:28.651 --> 37:30.254
You want to make
some music, huh?

37:30.390 --> 37:32.422
-(Bubbles grunts)
-(laughs)

37:32.557 --> 37:33.922
-(Bubbles screeches)
-(laughs)

37:34.058 --> 37:36.362
(hoots)

37:38.933 --> 37:39.955
That's me.

37:40.091 --> 37:42.164
I just released my new album.

37:42.300 --> 37:43.797
Those are my demos.

37:43.932 --> 37:46.064
(chuckling):
Don't mess that up.

37:47.373 --> 37:49.235
Here, I want to show you this.

37:49.370 --> 37:51.069
Look.

37:52.439 --> 37:54.305
Look.

37:54.441 --> 37:55.876
See?

37:57.116 --> 37:59.049
(Bubbles grunting)

37:59.184 --> 38:00.480
This is Neverland.

38:00.616 --> 38:03.015
I come here all the time.

38:04.653 --> 38:06.990
It's filled with magic,

38:07.125 --> 38:08.726
adventure,

38:08.862 --> 38:09.786
pirates.

38:09.922 --> 38:11.793
Here, I'll help you.

38:12.994 --> 38:15.368
-Look, the Lost Boys.
-(hoots softly)

38:20.673 --> 38:23.138
This is my favorite page.
It's Peter Pan.

38:23.273 --> 38:25.774
And his shadow.

38:27.541 --> 38:30.141
♪ ♪

38:42.688 --> 38:44.620
So, Michael.

38:45.356 --> 38:47.199
Surgeries. Have you had
any surgeries

38:47.334 --> 38:49.633
-in the past five years?
-Mm-mm.

38:51.605 --> 38:54.005
What about medications?
Are you taking any?

38:54.140 --> 38:55.671
No, ma'am.

38:55.806 --> 38:58.235
Just Benoquin cream
for my vitiligo.

38:59.145 --> 39:00.679
Oh, I'm sorry.

39:00.815 --> 39:03.449
You know, it's much more
common than people think.

39:04.513 --> 39:06.052
Has it spread?

39:06.187 --> 39:08.087
-A little bit.
-Yeah?

39:08.222 --> 39:10.012
Yeah. But, you know, the cream,

39:10.147 --> 39:11.917
it helps even out my skin tone.

39:12.053 --> 39:13.490
-NURSE: Oh, I see, yeah.
-(door opens)

39:13.626 --> 39:15.560
DOCTOR: Michael,
good to see you again.

39:15.695 --> 39:17.490
We're almost ready for you.
Any, uh...

39:17.626 --> 39:18.723
Any last questions?

39:18.858 --> 39:20.424
Oh, no. I'm ready.

39:20.560 --> 39:23.029
All right. I need to make
a few marks around the nose.

39:26.806 --> 39:29.031
You know, you're a pretty
good-looking kid.

39:29.167 --> 39:30.475
You sure you want to do this?

39:30.611 --> 39:33.212
(chuckles):
I'm not a kid anymore.

39:33.347 --> 39:35.743
And my nose is... it's too big.

39:35.879 --> 39:38.215
Hmm. I'm not sure that's true.

39:38.784 --> 39:41.318
Well, you see,
my face isn't symmetrical

39:41.453 --> 39:43.555
for the photographs and all.

39:44.356 --> 39:46.124
I have to be perfect.

39:46.260 --> 39:48.520
Well, you're the boss.

39:48.655 --> 39:50.529
Just relax.

39:56.169 --> 39:57.762
(hinges creaking)

39:57.898 --> 40:00.132
(vacuum machine whirring)

40:26.131 --> 40:27.733
Hey!

40:28.302 --> 40:30.162
What's going on, son?

40:31.499 --> 40:33.297
Son?

40:34.909 --> 40:36.476
Michael?

40:40.773 --> 40:43.615
Boy, come here.

40:52.656 --> 40:54.455
(sputtering):
What?

40:54.590 --> 40:56.122
What in the world?

40:58.430 --> 40:59.963
Let me see something.

41:00.099 --> 41:01.457
Hey.

41:08.999 --> 41:11.005
Oh, my God.

41:12.342 --> 41:13.975
Michael.

41:15.008 --> 41:17.044
It's for my sinuses.

41:30.696 --> 41:33.027
("Dreamer"
by The Jacksons playing)

41:35.295 --> 41:37.427
-(scoffing in disbelief)
-(door opens)

41:38.370 --> 41:40.071
(door closes)

41:40.206 --> 41:42.399
♪ ♪

41:48.749 --> 41:53.910
♪ I guess I'll always be
a dreamer ♪

41:54.046 --> 41:55.688
(Bubbles chattering)

41:56.457 --> 41:59.149
♪ Dreaming my life away... ♪

41:59.284 --> 42:02.727
♪ Dreaming my life away ♪

42:04.190 --> 42:07.792
♪ And nothing comes but sleep ♪

42:07.927 --> 42:11.731
♪ To a dreamer ♪

42:11.867 --> 42:14.901
♪ And when you wake up ♪

42:15.037 --> 42:19.579
♪ The dream is gone away... ♪

42:20.379 --> 42:21.779
(music stops)

42:21.914 --> 42:24.083
LA TOYA: Maybe I should
 get a nose job.

42:24.218 --> 42:26.182
(Michael chuckles)

42:26.751 --> 42:29.521
-You think so?
-Yes, I do.

42:29.657 --> 42:31.621
Muscles says,
"Everybody does it."

42:31.757 --> 42:33.689
-Mm-hmm.
-All the big stars.

42:33.824 --> 42:35.722
All our favorite ones.
(laughs)

42:35.857 --> 42:37.322
Well, it looks great.

42:38.422 --> 42:40.798
-You really think so?
-I do.

42:42.131 --> 42:44.502
-See, I wanted a new look.
-Oh, yeah?

42:44.637 --> 42:46.905
-Reinvent myself.
-Mm-hmm.

42:47.041 --> 42:50.071
You know, now that I'm doing
my own thing and...

42:51.371 --> 42:53.604
I want the world
to see me differently.

42:54.407 --> 42:57.144
Not a boy
in a kid band anymore.

42:57.779 --> 42:59.212
LA TOYA:
Yeah.

42:59.347 --> 43:02.578
Look around, Michael,
your fans love you.

43:03.624 --> 43:05.116
MICHAEL:
They're not my fans.

43:05.251 --> 43:07.286
They're part of my family.

43:08.596 --> 43:11.156
It's just time for me to start

43:11.292 --> 43:13.165
taking control
of my own destiny.

43:13.300 --> 43:14.627
LA TOYA:
Mm-hmm.

43:14.762 --> 43:16.159
You know?

43:16.295 --> 43:17.832
I want to be who I want to be.

43:17.967 --> 43:19.701
-(door opens)
-MARLON: Mikey.

43:19.837 --> 43:22.268
Joseph just called a meeting.

43:23.741 --> 43:25.104
Careful, he's hungry.

43:25.239 --> 43:27.108
-LA TOYA: How hungry?
-(sighs)

43:27.243 --> 43:29.407
(inhales deeply)
He's pretty hungry.

43:30.318 --> 43:31.778
For, like, a mouse?

43:31.914 --> 43:33.983
(chuckles)
Maybe.

43:36.153 --> 43:37.980
JOSEPH:
 There he is! Man of the hour!

43:38.115 --> 43:40.055
Man of the hour.

43:41.693 --> 43:43.696
Go on, sit down. Sit down.

43:48.026 --> 43:49.867
Ah. Now...

43:50.002 --> 43:52.403
you all real happy
about Michael's success.

43:52.539 --> 43:54.372
That's lovely to see.

43:54.508 --> 43:56.303
It's heartwarming.

43:56.438 --> 43:58.869
I mean, he can go all the way,
right to the top.

43:59.004 --> 44:00.944
All by himself.

44:02.014 --> 44:03.846
Wouldn't that be something?
Oh, man.

44:03.981 --> 44:07.317
Let me tell you,
the Jackson family

44:07.453 --> 44:09.750
is the brand.

44:09.886 --> 44:12.085
That's our Coca-Cola.

44:12.221 --> 44:15.317
Yeah. So we need
to open up the store

44:15.453 --> 44:17.156
and start selling. (chuckling)

44:17.291 --> 44:18.997
Or you know
what's gonna happen?

44:19.133 --> 44:20.594
Folks are gonna go out there
and start buying some Pepsi.

44:20.729 --> 44:22.428
(chuckling)

44:22.563 --> 44:25.738
We got to get in there again
and vend the wares.

44:26.606 --> 44:29.467
So, I've decided...

44:31.472 --> 44:35.178
...I'm arranging a tour
and a live album.

44:35.314 --> 44:37.046
(sighs)

44:38.348 --> 44:40.047
Wait, how are we gonna tour
without Jermaine?

44:40.183 --> 44:41.411
JOSEPH:
Your brother made his choice

44:41.547 --> 44:42.783
when we left Motown,
and he stayed.

44:42.918 --> 44:44.583
Let him live with it.

44:44.719 --> 44:48.517
The point is, we need to
capitalize on Michael's album.

44:48.653 --> 44:50.723
So, we gonna do
a bunch of songs...

44:50.858 --> 44:52.523
Joseph, I...

44:54.094 --> 44:56.334
I... I need to think.

44:56.469 --> 44:57.666
JOSEPH:
No, sir.

44:57.802 --> 44:59.871
I told you what to think.

45:00.974 --> 45:02.433
You got a problem
with that, Michael?

45:02.569 --> 45:04.232
We need to have
a reasonable conversation

45:04.368 --> 45:05.876
about this, Joseph.

45:06.012 --> 45:07.373
You think now
because you're a big

45:07.508 --> 45:09.179
superstar and you have
this big hit album

45:09.315 --> 45:10.281
that you're better
than everybody in this house?

45:10.416 --> 45:11.978
Is that it?

45:12.114 --> 45:13.912
You better than your brothers?

45:14.048 --> 45:16.155
Your mother and me?

45:16.290 --> 45:17.883
Is that it?

45:18.018 --> 45:20.155
You need to think.

45:21.357 --> 45:22.789
You think you're better
than me, boy?

45:22.925 --> 45:24.454
Joseph, that is enough.

45:24.589 --> 45:26.722
JOSEPH:
Is that it, Michael? Huh?

45:26.857 --> 45:28.560
-Is that it?
-KATHERINE: That is enough!

45:28.696 --> 45:30.432
("Doggin' Around"
by Michael Jackson playing)

45:30.567 --> 45:31.435
-♪ You better stop ♪
-JOSEPH: Katherine, sit down.

45:31.570 --> 45:35.401
♪ Your... ♪

45:36.069 --> 45:37.608
♪ Dog... ♪

45:37.744 --> 45:38.974
MICHAEL:
Let's go.

45:39.110 --> 45:42.746
♪ ...gin', ...gin' around ♪

45:42.881 --> 45:46.350
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah ♪

45:46.485 --> 45:48.151
(car door opens)

45:48.287 --> 45:51.246
♪ 'Cause if you
don't stop, I'm... ♪

45:51.382 --> 45:52.581
Where do you want to go?

45:52.716 --> 45:54.855
-Just drive.
-♪ Gonna ♪

45:54.991 --> 45:56.954
♪ Have to put you down ♪

45:57.089 --> 45:58.831
(engine starts)

46:00.561 --> 46:03.425
♪ Bah, bah, bah, bah,
bah, bah, bah ♪

46:03.560 --> 46:05.064
(people shouting and clamoring)

46:05.200 --> 46:07.430
♪ I can't take it ♪

46:07.565 --> 46:09.099
♪ Bah, bah, bah, bah ♪

46:09.234 --> 46:11.099
♪ Much longer ♪

46:11.235 --> 46:13.169
-♪ Bah, bah, bah, bah ♪
-(people shouting excitedly)

46:13.304 --> 46:15.339
-♪ My heart's getting weak ♪
-WOMAN: I love you, Michael!

46:15.474 --> 46:16.981
♪ Bah, bah, bah, bah ♪

46:17.117 --> 46:18.980
♪ It's not getting
any stronger ♪

46:19.115 --> 46:20.177
♪ Bah, bah, bah, bah ♪

46:20.313 --> 46:22.819
♪ You keep me so upset ♪

46:22.954 --> 46:24.348
♪ Bah, bah, bah, bah ♪

46:24.483 --> 46:27.153
♪ My head's in a whirl ♪

46:27.288 --> 46:28.451
♪ Bah, bah, bah, bah ♪

46:28.586 --> 46:31.429
♪ But if you want to be, yeah ♪

46:31.565 --> 46:34.697
♪ Be my girl ♪

46:34.833 --> 46:36.499
♪ You better stop ♪

46:36.634 --> 46:39.033
♪ Your ♪

46:39.168 --> 46:44.802
♪ Dog...gin' around ♪

46:44.938 --> 46:47.236
♪ You know what
I'm talkin' 'bout, yeah ♪

46:47.372 --> 46:49.310
♪ Yeah, yeah ♪

46:50.943 --> 46:56.418
♪ If you don't stop,
I'm gonna... ♪

46:56.554 --> 46:58.985
MICHAEL: I'm so sick of it,
 Bill. All of it.

46:59.121 --> 47:01.355
Joseph's exploiting me.

47:02.453 --> 47:04.187
I had a whole plan.

47:04.323 --> 47:07.031
Track list, the visuals.

47:08.031 --> 47:10.793
I wanted to do a solo tour.

47:13.305 --> 47:15.902
He's just...
he's just ruining it all.

47:16.037 --> 47:17.701
He's just...

47:18.404 --> 47:20.671
(bird calling in distance)

47:22.340 --> 47:23.949
I need my freedom.

47:24.813 --> 47:26.385
Well...

47:26.520 --> 47:28.547
You can move out.

47:29.921 --> 47:31.990
I'm not ready for that.

47:35.729 --> 47:37.556
It's not that easy.

47:37.691 --> 47:41.494
Life's not easy, son.
I'll tell you.

47:47.233 --> 47:49.073
I love my family.

47:50.740 --> 47:52.208
I do.

47:55.675 --> 47:58.541
(sighs):
I just want to do my own thing.

47:58.676 --> 48:00.909
Joseph's never gonna change.

48:01.045 --> 48:04.046
Only thing he cares about
is the Jackson family.

48:04.182 --> 48:05.381
Huh?

48:05.517 --> 48:07.258
And no matter what you do,

48:07.393 --> 48:10.726
he's only ever gonna see it
as a family success.

48:10.861 --> 48:13.191
Get your own team.

48:13.326 --> 48:15.400
Get you a good lawyer.

48:15.535 --> 48:17.427
Think about it.

48:17.562 --> 48:20.467
("Ben" by The Jacksons playing)

48:25.308 --> 48:29.444
♪ Ben,
the two of us need look ♪

48:29.580 --> 48:32.608
-♪ No more ♪
-(cheering, screaming loudly)

48:32.744 --> 48:36.246
♪ We both found what we were ♪

48:36.381 --> 48:39.550
♪ Looking for ♪

48:39.685 --> 48:44.586
♪ With a friend
to call my own ♪

48:44.722 --> 48:48.427
♪ I'll never be alone ♪

48:48.562 --> 48:52.530
♪ And you,
my friend, will see ♪

48:52.666 --> 48:55.674
♪ You've got a friend in me ♪

48:55.810 --> 48:58.201
(cheering, screaming continue)

48:58.336 --> 49:00.607
♪ ♪

49:01.977 --> 49:05.782
-♪ Ben, you're always running ♪
-(speaking indistinctly)

49:05.918 --> 49:09.019
♪ Here and there ♪

49:09.155 --> 49:13.250
♪ You feel you're not wanted ♪

49:13.385 --> 49:16.586
♪ Anywhere ♪

49:16.721 --> 49:21.790
♪ If you ever look behind ♪

49:21.926 --> 49:25.468
♪ And don't like
what you find ♪

49:25.604 --> 49:27.672
-♪ There's something ♪
-(cheering, screaming)

49:27.808 --> 49:29.336
♪ You should know ♪

49:29.472 --> 49:34.178
♪ You've got a place to go ♪

49:39.511 --> 49:44.518
♪ Like Ben. ♪

49:46.659 --> 49:47.888
(song ends)

49:48.023 --> 49:51.327
♪ ♪

49:52.194 --> 49:53.659
(elevator bell dings)

49:58.700 --> 50:01.229
SENIOR PARTNER:
So, we appreciate you coming in

50:01.365 --> 50:05.001
and we applaud your decision
to seek independent counsel.

50:05.136 --> 50:07.504
We can assure you the most
comprehensive attention

50:07.639 --> 50:09.346
to your entire media portfolio.

50:09.481 --> 50:11.510
SENIOR PARTNER 2:
At Hardee, Barovick, we believe

50:11.645 --> 50:13.075
in treating our clients
as family

50:13.210 --> 50:15.252
-and we want you to--
-I already have a family.

50:17.022 --> 50:18.552
MAN:
Too much of one.

50:20.459 --> 50:23.061
I mean, the whole point's
going solo, right?

50:23.196 --> 50:24.855
So, that means
you're probably gonna

50:24.990 --> 50:27.462
break a few hearts
over there in Encino.

50:31.037 --> 50:33.237
Unless I'm missing something.

50:40.479 --> 50:43.044
-Do I know you?
-MAN: No, I don't think so.

50:43.180 --> 50:45.081
MICHAEL:
You sure?

50:45.216 --> 50:47.882
Yeah. I think I'd remember.

50:48.017 --> 50:49.950
Who are you?

50:50.085 --> 50:52.047
John Branca.

50:53.492 --> 50:55.825
-You handle The Beach Boys.
-BRANCA: Yeah, I do.

50:55.961 --> 50:57.491
Neil Diamond, Bob Dylan,

50:57.627 --> 50:59.989
couple other guys,
and now I work here.

51:00.801 --> 51:02.158
I like The Beach Boys.

51:02.294 --> 51:03.295
Me, too.

51:03.431 --> 51:04.928
Brian Wilson's a genius.

51:05.064 --> 51:07.403
Some of the best harmonies
in rock and roll.

51:11.377 --> 51:13.205
You know what
I'm after, Mr. Branca?

51:13.340 --> 51:14.444
BRANCA:
Sure.

51:15.514 --> 51:17.644
You want to be
the biggest star in the world.

51:21.582 --> 51:23.617
Can you help make that happen?

51:24.525 --> 51:25.817
Yes.

51:26.890 --> 51:28.149
How?

51:29.252 --> 51:32.956
Because I believe
there's no one like you.

51:33.966 --> 51:36.333
And there never will be.

51:44.143 --> 51:46.002
SENIOR PARTNER:
Mr. Jackson...

51:47.043 --> 51:48.277
Mr. Jackson,

51:48.413 --> 51:50.644
-I apologize--
-He's my guy.

51:54.815 --> 51:57.288
Can you leave us alone
for a second?

51:57.954 --> 51:59.648
Please.

51:59.784 --> 52:01.283
MAN 1:
Of course.

52:01.419 --> 52:03.118
Yes.

52:07.965 --> 52:10.169
(door opens)

52:13.565 --> 52:14.838
(door closes)

52:14.973 --> 52:16.934
Okay, Mr. Branca.

52:17.069 --> 52:20.509
-(clears throat)
-Here's your first job.

52:22.345 --> 52:24.843
I need you to fire Joseph.

52:26.445 --> 52:28.018
Your dad?

52:28.154 --> 52:30.046
You want me to fire your dad?

52:31.149 --> 52:33.522
And how would you
like me to do that?

52:34.386 --> 52:35.660
Quickly.

52:35.795 --> 52:37.420
♪ ♪

52:37.555 --> 52:39.726
(plucking notes)

52:40.692 --> 52:42.927
(machine beeps, whirs)

53:03.156 --> 53:04.921
-Yes.
-I think it goes...

53:05.057 --> 53:06.220
Button it up like this.

53:06.355 --> 53:07.554
-Oh, right.
-Yeah.

53:07.690 --> 53:10.086
La Toya, get the hell on
out of here.

53:11.327 --> 53:13.293
Kate, look at this.

53:13.428 --> 53:14.693
Will you look at this?

53:14.829 --> 53:17.336
The boy fired me
with a piece of paper.

53:17.471 --> 53:20.037
A piece of-- Couldn't
even be man-to-man, huh?

53:20.173 --> 53:22.672
Look me in the eye and do it.

53:22.808 --> 53:24.738
That boy's gonna feel my belt
when he get in here!

53:25.802 --> 53:27.169
No, he's not.

53:28.238 --> 53:30.379
-Yes, the hell he is.
-No, he's not.

53:30.515 --> 53:32.476
What are you gonna do,
beat him?

53:32.612 --> 53:35.050
You gonna whup him?

53:35.185 --> 53:36.613
He's grown.

53:36.749 --> 53:38.455
What'd you say to me?

53:40.787 --> 53:43.394
I said you can't do it no more.

53:44.229 --> 53:46.364
You can't whup nobody.

53:47.760 --> 53:49.631
You can't beat nobody.

53:51.229 --> 53:54.196
And if you don't like it,
you can leave.

53:59.379 --> 54:00.812
And the next time
you see your son,

54:00.948 --> 54:02.742
you ought to thank him.

54:02.877 --> 54:04.577
Everything we have
is because of him

54:04.712 --> 54:06.511
and don't you ever forget that.

54:06.647 --> 54:08.077
Everybody seems to forget

54:08.213 --> 54:11.180
that I'm the one
that got us out of Gary.

54:12.884 --> 54:15.255
And everything I've done

54:15.391 --> 54:17.426
is for this family.

54:17.562 --> 54:20.827
You go on ahead
and keep thinking that.

54:22.936 --> 54:25.667
(leaves rustling)

54:27.973 --> 54:29.340
(giraffe grunts)

54:29.476 --> 54:31.974
("Enjoy Yourself"
by The Jacksons playing)

54:32.910 --> 54:34.839
♪ Enjoy yourself,
 enjoy yourself ♪

54:34.974 --> 54:37.174
♪ Enjoy yourself with me ♪

54:37.310 --> 54:39.117
♪ Enjoy yourself,
 enjoy yourself ♪

54:39.252 --> 54:41.317
♪ Enjoy yourself with me ♪

54:41.453 --> 54:44.147
♪ You better enjoy yourself ♪

54:45.857 --> 54:47.885
-(loud pop)
-♪ You better enjoy yourself ♪

54:48.020 --> 54:50.255
-(Michael laughing)
-(toy squeaks)

54:51.091 --> 54:52.960
MICHAEL:
 You didn't go down this side.

54:53.096 --> 54:55.667
-Left.
-Where? This? Left?
Going left. All right.

54:55.803 --> 54:58.001
-(train whistle blows)
-♪ While people are dancin' ♪

54:58.136 --> 55:00.595
-♪ Dancin' all over the place ♪
-BILL: A little
choo choo train.

55:00.731 --> 55:03.135
-MICHAEL: I love it.
-♪ But you shouldn't worry ♪

55:03.271 --> 55:05.236
-♪ About things you
can't control ♪
-MICHAEL: Hi.

55:05.371 --> 55:07.673
♪ Come on, girl,
while the night is young... ♪

55:07.808 --> 55:09.170
Yeah. So, I'm really excited.

55:09.306 --> 55:10.412
-This looks really cool.
-(music stops)

55:10.547 --> 55:11.878
MICHAEL:
That's you.

55:12.013 --> 55:12.984
BOY: I can't wait
to start playing it.

55:13.120 --> 55:14.318
That's Michael Jackson.

55:14.454 --> 55:15.379
-What?
-It's Michael Jackson.

55:15.514 --> 55:16.685
What?!

55:17.719 --> 55:19.149
Please excuse him. (chuckles)

55:19.285 --> 55:22.125
Are-Are you, um,
are you actually, really...

55:22.261 --> 55:23.854
Yeah, I'm Michael, yeah.

55:23.989 --> 55:25.687
-Wow.
-Mom, it's...

55:25.822 --> 55:26.888
I wonder...

55:27.024 --> 55:28.627
I'd love an autograph.

55:28.763 --> 55:30.729
For my son, I mean. (chuckles)

55:30.864 --> 55:33.135
-Honey?
-Of course, yeah. Um...

55:33.270 --> 55:35.498
He's a huge fan.

55:35.633 --> 55:37.002
Here.

55:37.138 --> 55:38.937
How about I sign this?
What's your name?

55:39.072 --> 55:41.778
Uh, you can just
make it out to Pauline.

55:41.914 --> 55:43.204
Mom?

55:43.340 --> 55:45.040
-Pauline. (chuckles)
-BOY: Mom, Mom.

55:45.176 --> 55:47.012
Mom, my name's Max,
not Pauline.

55:47.147 --> 55:48.548
-I'm-I'm not Pauline.
-(shushing)

55:48.683 --> 55:50.547
Is that the new Atari game?

55:51.217 --> 55:52.649
-I love that.
-You've played it?

55:52.785 --> 55:54.724
Oh, yeah, all the time.

55:54.859 --> 55:57.721
Just be sure to keep
toggling left when you fire.

55:57.857 --> 55:59.661
That's how you power up.

55:59.797 --> 56:01.695
-Cool. Thank you.
-MICHAEL: Of course.

56:01.831 --> 56:03.162
("Enjoy Yourself"
resumes playing)

56:03.298 --> 56:04.733
Hi.

56:04.869 --> 56:06.798
-Would you like an autograph?
-Yes, please.

56:06.933 --> 56:08.866
-What's your name?
-Anika.

56:09.001 --> 56:10.575
Anika. That's a pretty name.

56:10.710 --> 56:12.738
-MAN: What do you say, baby?
-ANIKA: Thank you.

56:12.873 --> 56:14.706
WOMAN:
We're huge fans.

56:14.842 --> 56:16.738
MICHAEL:
Thank you so much.

56:16.874 --> 56:18.450
-♪ Enjoy yourself ♪
-♪ Let's get on down ♪

56:18.585 --> 56:19.977
-♪ Enjoy yourself ♪
-Thanks.

56:20.113 --> 56:22.286
MICHAEL:
Hey, everybody. Too cute.

56:22.422 --> 56:24.385
-(music stops)
-(chattering)

56:24.520 --> 56:25.553
Over here, over here.

56:25.688 --> 56:27.888
-Get open.
-(chattering)

56:29.359 --> 56:30.759
(net rattles)

56:32.392 --> 56:34.056
-BILL: Here, here, I got it.
-(brothers chattering)

56:34.192 --> 56:35.765
-Hey.
-JERMAINE: Hey, Mikey.

56:35.901 --> 56:37.093
-MARLON: What's up, Mikey?
-All right, jokers.

56:37.228 --> 56:38.334
MARLON AND TITO:
What's up, Bill?

56:38.469 --> 56:39.994
(peacock cawing in distance)

56:40.130 --> 56:41.006
-Ah!
-Too short.

56:41.141 --> 56:43.669
(brothers chattering)

56:43.804 --> 56:45.141
MICHAEL:
Guys, look!

56:45.276 --> 56:46.676
I got Twister.

56:46.811 --> 56:48.477
 -Twister?
-You want to play tonight?

56:48.612 --> 56:49.909
-Michael, Twister?
-Really?

56:50.044 --> 56:51.307
What we gonna do
with Twister, man?

56:51.442 --> 56:52.814
Come on.
It'll be like the old days.

56:52.949 --> 56:54.377
Would love to, Mike,
but I got to be home

56:54.512 --> 56:56.049
with the family.
I can't be playing games.

56:56.184 --> 56:57.788
MARLON: And the rest of us
are going out tonight.

56:57.923 --> 56:59.490
-TITO: Yeah,
Marlon's got a hot date.
-MARLON: Yeah.

56:59.626 --> 57:01.053
-(brothers laughing)
-Marlon, what time

57:01.188 --> 57:03.058
are you gonna be home?
We could play then.

57:03.193 --> 57:05.124
Hey, Marlon's gonna be playing
his own game of Twister.

57:05.259 --> 57:06.597
-(brothers exclaim)
-MARLON: Shut up, Jackie.

57:06.732 --> 57:08.330
-I'm always lucky.
-(brothers laugh)

57:08.466 --> 57:09.827
JACKIE:
Yeah, right.

57:09.962 --> 57:11.426
You guys are no fun anymore.

57:11.562 --> 57:13.594
JERMAINE: Come on, Mike.
Don't be like that.

57:13.730 --> 57:15.666
("Blame It on the Boogie"
by The Jacksons playing)

57:15.802 --> 57:17.108
(Bubbles chattering)

57:17.244 --> 57:18.475
Hey, that's cheating.

57:18.610 --> 57:20.672
You got red, not green.
(laughing)

57:20.807 --> 57:23.042
♪ My baby's always dancin'
and it wouldn't
be a bad thing ♪

57:23.177 --> 57:24.774
♪ But I don't get
no lovin'... ♪

57:24.909 --> 57:26.810
It's okay.

57:26.946 --> 57:28.582
Don't worry about it.

57:28.718 --> 57:30.589
It takes a long time to learn

57:30.724 --> 57:33.855
-and I'm a professional dancer.
-(chattering)

57:34.722 --> 57:36.154
You want some ice cream?

57:36.290 --> 57:37.692
♪ Don't blame it
on the sunshine... ♪

57:37.828 --> 57:38.855
Okay, but then
I've got to go to work.

57:38.991 --> 57:41.164
Don't break anything.

57:41.299 --> 57:42.626
I'll be back.

57:42.761 --> 57:44.030
(chattering)

57:44.166 --> 57:45.836
♪ Don't blame it
on the sunshine ♪

57:45.972 --> 57:48.200
-♪ Don't blame it
on the moonlight ♪
-(hooting)

57:48.335 --> 57:50.465
♪ Don't blame it
on the good times ♪

57:50.600 --> 57:52.406
♪ Blame it on the boogie,
whoo... ♪

57:52.542 --> 57:53.835
(Bubbles screeching)

57:53.970 --> 57:56.113
♪ ♪

57:56.248 --> 57:58.550
(Michael humming)

58:01.347 --> 58:04.050
-(music stops abruptly)
-(Michael gasps softly)

58:08.253 --> 58:10.628
I was thinking
about framing this.

58:16.728 --> 58:17.998
Read it.

58:19.699 --> 58:22.398
Go on. Read it.

58:27.005 --> 58:28.877
Firing your own father.

58:29.745 --> 58:31.847
What kind of son does that?

58:37.521 --> 58:39.723
(sighs)
Michael...

58:42.255 --> 58:44.596
You got a lot to learn
about family.

58:54.372 --> 58:56.105
(door slams shut)

58:56.240 --> 58:57.441
-("The Love You Save" playing)
-♪ Stop, na, na, na ♪

58:57.576 --> 59:00.042
♪ You'd better save it ♪

59:00.177 --> 59:03.939
♪ Stop, stop, stop,
you'd better save it ♪

59:04.074 --> 59:05.511
♪ Whoo... ♪

59:05.646 --> 59:08.244
(vocalizing)

59:08.380 --> 59:10.288
-Hi. Welcome back, Michael.
-Hi.

59:10.423 --> 59:12.390
MICHAEL:
Beautiful name.

59:12.525 --> 59:13.889
PHOTOGRAPHER:
Look up for us.

59:14.025 --> 59:14.984
♪ When we played tag
in grade school ♪

59:15.120 --> 59:16.451
♪ You wanted to be it ♪

59:16.587 --> 59:17.925
-MICHAEL: This is for you.
-(giggling)

59:18.061 --> 59:19.488
♪ But chasing boys
was just a fad ♪

59:19.624 --> 59:21.597
♪ You crossed your heart
you'd quit ♪

59:21.733 --> 59:23.830
♪ When we grew up you traded ♪

59:23.965 --> 59:25.800
♪ Your promise for my ring ♪

59:25.936 --> 59:27.672
PHOTOGRAPHER:
Michael, over here.

59:27.807 --> 59:29.773
♪ You're doing
the same old thing... ♪

59:29.909 --> 59:32.934
You want to say that again,
transistor face?

59:33.070 --> 59:35.541
You watch TV?

59:35.676 --> 59:38.115
Yeah. Sometimes.

59:38.251 --> 59:40.408
You watch TV?

59:40.544 --> 59:42.614
-Yeah.
-(TV continues indistinctly)

59:42.749 --> 59:44.283
Cartoons.

59:44.952 --> 59:46.856
 Three Stooges a lot.

59:47.886 --> 59:49.952
Charlie Chaplin.

59:50.088 --> 59:51.553
You know who he is?

59:52.323 --> 59:54.663
-Duh.
-No, you don't.

59:54.798 --> 59:57.163
You're such a doo-doo head.

59:58.163 --> 01:00:00.167
He's wonderful, really.

01:00:00.302 --> 01:00:03.466
He's an actor,
he's a movie director...

01:00:04.135 --> 01:00:06.007
...and he writes songs.

01:00:07.577 --> 01:00:09.676
I have a dog.

01:00:09.811 --> 01:00:11.146
It's a dachshund.

01:00:11.282 --> 01:00:12.909
Mm.

01:00:13.044 --> 01:00:14.513
What's his name?

01:00:14.648 --> 01:00:15.517
Rudy.

01:00:15.652 --> 01:00:17.345
He's getting fat.

01:00:17.480 --> 01:00:19.886
My mom says
I feed him too much.

01:00:20.021 --> 01:00:22.227
(chuckling):
I love Rudy.

01:00:22.362 --> 01:00:24.061
Do you have any pets?

01:00:24.196 --> 01:00:26.055
Uh...

01:00:26.190 --> 01:00:29.395
a snake and a giraffe.

01:00:29.531 --> 01:00:30.827
No way.

01:00:30.962 --> 01:00:31.996
And a llama.

01:00:32.132 --> 01:00:34.431
(indistinct P.A. announcement)

01:00:34.566 --> 01:00:37.868
(muffled): And three parrots,
two spiders,

01:00:38.004 --> 01:00:40.211
and a whole lot of dogs.

01:00:40.346 --> 01:00:42.672
(low conversation)

01:00:43.342 --> 01:00:44.849
MICHAEL:
 It's got to be

01:00:44.984 --> 01:00:46.344
 the greatest-selling album
 of all time.

01:00:47.312 --> 01:00:48.816
And not just by a Black artist

01:00:48.951 --> 01:00:52.319
but by any race,
any color, okay?

01:00:52.455 --> 01:00:55.325
Then I want the-the largest
concert tour there ever was.

01:00:55.461 --> 01:00:56.759
Just stadiums only.

01:00:56.894 --> 01:00:58.656
Just thousands
and thousands of people

01:00:58.791 --> 01:01:01.833
just rushing into the stadiums
and just all over the world.

01:01:01.968 --> 01:01:05.160
I also want to make short films
featuring my music.

01:01:05.295 --> 01:01:06.368
That's ambitious.

01:01:06.504 --> 01:01:07.701
I can see it.

01:01:07.837 --> 01:01:09.340
You see it. You can do it.

01:01:09.476 --> 01:01:12.173
And I-I see it so clearly.

01:01:12.876 --> 01:01:14.304
Well, Walter Yetnikoff called.

01:01:14.440 --> 01:01:16.045
CBS wants
to do a press release.

01:01:16.180 --> 01:01:20.884
No. No, no press,
no, no interviews, no nothing.

01:01:21.654 --> 01:01:23.414
He's not gonna like that.

01:01:24.150 --> 01:01:26.186
You got to handle that, Branca.

01:01:26.820 --> 01:01:28.556
You see...

01:01:28.692 --> 01:01:30.755
I want to be mysterious.

01:01:30.890 --> 01:01:32.121
Like-like Garbo.

01:01:32.256 --> 01:01:34.228
You know, like, uh...

01:01:34.363 --> 01:01:36.757
I mean, if Halley's Comet
came every year,

01:01:36.893 --> 01:01:40.035
just year after year,
would you look at it?

01:01:41.806 --> 01:01:43.369
You're gonna need publicity.

01:01:43.505 --> 01:01:46.535
What I'm gonna need is
a good record that sells.

01:01:46.670 --> 01:01:48.605
-Nothing else matters.
-Fair enough.

01:01:48.741 --> 01:01:52.476
Then I suggest you start
laying down some killer demos.

01:01:53.077 --> 01:01:54.477
Can you do that?

01:01:54.613 --> 01:01:56.918
(chuckles):
Of course, I can do that.

01:01:57.054 --> 01:01:58.212
("Think Happy"
by The Jacksons playing)

01:01:58.347 --> 01:02:00.719
(scatting quietly)

01:02:01.421 --> 01:02:03.888
(laughs):
What are you doing, Mike?

01:02:04.023 --> 01:02:05.930
I'm channeling.

01:02:06.066 --> 01:02:09.057
I'm letting the Creator
give me a song right now.

01:02:09.827 --> 01:02:13.262
But if I'm not here
to receive these ideas,

01:02:13.398 --> 01:02:15.966
God might give them to Prince.

01:02:16.102 --> 01:02:18.633
(brothers laughing)

01:02:18.769 --> 01:02:20.276
TITO:
You're ticking me off, man.

01:02:20.411 --> 01:02:21.169
Tito.

01:02:21.305 --> 01:02:23.137
(vocalizing in song)

01:02:23.273 --> 01:02:27.780
♪ There ain't no reason, hah,
for you to be sad, yeah ♪

01:02:27.915 --> 01:02:29.810
(Michael scatting)

01:02:29.946 --> 01:02:32.320
-♪ I know things can't be ♪
-Hello.

01:02:32.456 --> 01:02:34.456
-♪ They can't be that bad ♪
-(llama braying)

01:02:34.591 --> 01:02:36.454
♪ Yeah ♪

01:02:37.788 --> 01:02:40.087
JACKIE:
♪ With a smile on your face ♪

01:02:40.223 --> 01:02:41.657
-(llama brays)
-MICHAEL:
♪ Smile on your face ♪

01:02:41.792 --> 01:02:43.658
JACKIE:
♪ With the love in your eyes ♪

01:02:43.793 --> 01:02:45.765
MICHAEL:
♪ Love in your eyes ♪

01:02:45.900 --> 01:02:47.903
-JACKIE: ♪ I know
you'll feel better ♪
-MICHAEL: ♪ Oh ♪

01:02:48.038 --> 01:02:51.272
ALL:
♪ You can only try ♪

01:02:51.407 --> 01:02:53.477
-♪ Try to think ♪
-♪ Happy ♪

01:02:53.613 --> 01:02:55.207
♪ Happy, happy ♪

01:02:55.343 --> 01:02:57.980
♪ That's the only way to be. ♪

01:02:58.116 --> 01:03:00.445
 -(Michael scatting)
-(song fades)

01:03:01.653 --> 01:03:04.317
(continues scatting)

01:03:05.952 --> 01:03:07.617
(stops scatting)

01:03:08.492 --> 01:03:09.757
Yeah.

01:03:09.893 --> 01:03:11.255
♪ Sing it to the world ♪

01:03:11.390 --> 01:03:12.989
♪ Sing it all night long ♪

01:03:13.124 --> 01:03:15.295
(humming)

01:03:15.995 --> 01:03:18.133
(scatting)

01:03:20.065 --> 01:03:21.466
(stops scatting)

01:03:27.675 --> 01:03:29.980
MAN (over TV): Almost all
of the gunfire and death

01:03:30.115 --> 01:03:33.917
over drugs and territory
involves rival gangs.

01:03:34.053 --> 01:03:36.855
Ryan Chavez reports
from Los Angeles.

01:03:36.990 --> 01:03:38.821
(woman sobbing
and speaking indistinctly)

01:03:38.957 --> 01:03:40.854
CHAVEZ:
 A best friend killed

01:03:40.990 --> 01:03:42.886
 by a rival gang member.

01:03:43.022 --> 01:03:45.325
 Another killed at a drive-by
 shooting in Sacramento,

01:03:45.460 --> 01:03:47.197
 because he wore
 the wrong color.

01:03:47.333 --> 01:03:50.226
 Those who wear blue
 call themselves the Crips,

01:03:50.362 --> 01:03:52.134
 the Bloods wear red.

01:03:52.269 --> 01:03:54.098
 Some, like Smokey,
 survive attacks,

01:03:54.233 --> 01:03:55.398
 though paralyzed.

01:03:55.533 --> 01:03:57.332
People dyin' over nothing, man.

01:03:57.468 --> 01:03:58.843
 Over a neighborhood.

01:03:58.978 --> 01:04:00.203
CHAVEZ:
 Yet, the city remains filled

01:04:00.338 --> 01:04:01.677
 with warring soldiers.

01:04:01.813 --> 01:04:03.843
It's easy to Crip to me.

01:04:03.978 --> 01:04:06.577
MAN: Something y'all don't do,
y'all don't watch out--

01:04:06.712 --> 01:04:08.246
You wouldn't die for him,
would you?

01:04:08.381 --> 01:04:09.745
You're saying that now on TV,

01:04:09.881 --> 01:04:10.985
but you wouldn't die
for him for real.

01:04:11.120 --> 01:04:12.755
Yeah, I'd die for my homeboy.

01:04:12.891 --> 01:04:15.487
MAN 2:
But as-as time went on,

01:04:15.622 --> 01:04:17.655
I started to get too deep
in the drugs,

01:04:17.790 --> 01:04:20.090
so I started getting
in trouble on the streets.

01:04:20.226 --> 01:04:21.724
So, I thought to myself,

01:04:21.859 --> 01:04:23.892
"You know,
it was either this or death."

01:04:24.027 --> 01:04:26.733
CHAVEZ: Ryan Chavez
reporting from Los Angeles.

01:04:26.868 --> 01:04:29.303
♪ ♪

01:04:33.571 --> 01:04:35.870
(fingers snapping repeatedly)

01:04:44.991 --> 01:04:48.883
-(snapping continues)
-(scatting)

01:04:56.803 --> 01:04:58.827
(clicking tongue rhythmically)

01:05:00.235 --> 01:05:02.765
(clicking tongue rhythmically)

01:05:04.874 --> 01:05:06.567
(snapping fingers)

01:05:06.703 --> 01:05:08.474
(clicking tongue rhythmically)

01:05:12.079 --> 01:05:14.282
(snapping fingers)

01:05:18.248 --> 01:05:19.715
Hmm.

01:05:19.851 --> 01:05:22.092
 -(phone line ringing)
-♪ ♪

01:05:25.457 --> 01:05:26.721
BILL (on phone):
Hello?

01:05:26.857 --> 01:05:28.294
MICHAEL:
 Hey, Bill, it's me.

01:05:28.430 --> 01:05:29.999
BILL:
 Hey, Joker. What's up?

01:05:30.134 --> 01:05:31.828
MICHAEL:
 Well, I need some help

01:05:31.963 --> 01:05:34.005
 and was hoping
 you could pull some favors.

01:05:34.140 --> 01:05:36.470
BILL: Okay,
they're all at the studio.

01:05:36.605 --> 01:05:38.405
 But they're only there
 because of you.

01:05:39.508 --> 01:05:41.670
I can't believe
you're doing this.

01:05:41.806 --> 01:05:44.142
Music will bring
people together, Bill.

01:05:44.277 --> 01:05:46.082
That's the point.

01:05:46.218 --> 01:05:48.815
And if things work out,
I have a big idea.

01:05:48.950 --> 01:05:51.253
♪ ♪

01:05:53.225 --> 01:05:54.984
♪ California
knows how to party ♪

01:05:55.120 --> 01:05:56.687
-("West Coast Poplock" playing)
-(loud overlapping chatter)

01:05:56.822 --> 01:05:59.729
♪ California
knows how to party ♪

01:05:59.865 --> 01:06:01.192
(loud overlapping chatter)

01:06:01.328 --> 01:06:03.999
♪ In the city of L.A. ♪

01:06:04.134 --> 01:06:05.464
MAN:
What the hell is that?

01:06:05.600 --> 01:06:09.335
♪ In the city
of good old Watts ♪

01:06:09.470 --> 01:06:13.701
♪ In the city,
city of Compton ♪

01:06:13.836 --> 01:06:15.808
♪ They're poplocking ♪

01:06:16.511 --> 01:06:18.640
-Okay, Pete.
-(excited chattering)

01:06:18.776 --> 01:06:21.118
♪ Dance, dance, disco style ♪

01:06:21.253 --> 01:06:22.646
♪ It's all on
the West Coast... ♪

01:06:22.781 --> 01:06:24.955
Hold up. That's Michael.
Michael Jackson.

01:06:25.091 --> 01:06:27.319
-(excited chattering)
-(music stops)

01:06:27.455 --> 01:06:29.127
-Oh, shit.
-You really came.

01:06:29.262 --> 01:06:31.924
-He actually came.
-That was juicy right there.

01:06:32.060 --> 01:06:33.854
What was that?

01:06:33.990 --> 01:06:35.228
This dance is called
Popping, man.

01:06:35.363 --> 01:06:37.434
-(grunting)
-(all cheering)

01:06:37.569 --> 01:06:38.601
Whoo!

01:06:38.736 --> 01:06:40.863
Hey, and this...

01:06:41.664 --> 01:06:43.668
(overlapping chatter)

01:06:44.937 --> 01:06:46.677
-That's called the C-Walk, cuz.
-Yeah, hey.

01:06:46.812 --> 01:06:49.003
(overlapping chatter)

01:06:51.675 --> 01:06:53.677
Hey, can I get an autograph?

01:06:53.812 --> 01:06:55.383
-(Michael laughs)
-(others groaning)

01:06:57.114 --> 01:07:00.058
-Whatever, cuz.
Look, it's for my sister.
-Man!

01:07:00.193 --> 01:07:01.687
-Come on.
-MICHAEL: No, yeah, of course.

01:07:01.822 --> 01:07:04.458
Afterwards,
I'll sign autographs
for everybody.

01:07:05.192 --> 01:07:07.230
(excited chatter)

01:07:08.066 --> 01:07:10.124
(chuckles):
For sure.

01:07:10.259 --> 01:07:12.433
Look, I know this isn't easy
for you guys.

01:07:12.568 --> 01:07:14.267
So I just want to thank
everybody for coming.

01:07:14.402 --> 01:07:16.841
It's really important to me.

01:07:16.976 --> 01:07:19.370
You see,
I think music and dance

01:07:19.506 --> 01:07:21.838
is what we all have in common.

01:07:23.378 --> 01:07:25.242
That's a universal language.

01:07:25.377 --> 01:07:27.081
(others murmuring)

01:07:27.216 --> 01:07:28.444
And we can change the world.

01:07:28.580 --> 01:07:31.122
-I believe that.
-Word.

01:07:32.086 --> 01:07:33.957
Sounds good.

01:07:34.092 --> 01:07:36.452
Let's work on that together.

01:07:36.588 --> 01:07:38.285
 (snapping rhythmically)

01:07:38.421 --> 01:07:42.265
-(multiple fingers snapping)
-(feet stepping in rhythm)

01:07:44.727 --> 01:07:47.136
(grunts rhythmically)

01:07:47.271 --> 01:07:50.471
(quietly):
Bam. Bam. Bam. Yep.

01:07:54.604 --> 01:07:56.609
Bam. Bam. Bam.

01:08:03.612 --> 01:08:05.123
Keep going.

01:08:06.292 --> 01:08:08.451
Yeah, let's...
let's work on that part.

01:08:09.054 --> 01:08:10.752
Right now, let's just forget
about the arms.

01:08:10.887 --> 01:08:13.326
It... shouldn't be too forced.

01:08:13.462 --> 01:08:15.661
It's natural. It's a flow.

01:08:17.594 --> 01:08:18.829
All together.

01:08:19.539 --> 01:08:21.066
Ooh.

01:08:21.201 --> 01:08:22.835
(low murmuring)

01:08:22.971 --> 01:08:24.834
See?

01:08:24.969 --> 01:08:27.006
-It's in unison, you know.
-Yes.

01:08:27.141 --> 01:08:28.602
Think of, uh...

01:08:28.737 --> 01:08:30.242
a school of fish.

01:08:30.377 --> 01:08:31.609
You all move together.

01:08:31.745 --> 01:08:34.081
-You know what I mean?
-Yeah. Sure.

01:08:34.217 --> 01:08:36.280
I'm gonna try something.

01:08:36.415 --> 01:08:38.486
Just got an idea.

01:08:39.952 --> 01:08:42.290
Bill, can you bring
my jacket, please?

01:08:42.426 --> 01:08:44.520
I want to try something
while we...

01:08:44.655 --> 01:08:46.989
travel down this ways.

01:08:47.624 --> 01:08:49.398
The jacket...

01:08:50.298 --> 01:08:52.170
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

01:08:53.136 --> 01:08:54.634
Let's do it again.

01:08:54.769 --> 01:08:56.063
I'm gonna break out
and do something

01:08:56.199 --> 01:08:58.572
but continue with that...
with that flow.

01:09:03.275 --> 01:09:04.710
Ooh.

01:09:06.413 --> 01:09:08.781
(others exclaiming)

01:09:09.651 --> 01:09:11.783
-(exclaiming)
-Yeah, I like it.

01:09:14.984 --> 01:09:16.990
-All day.
-Yeah. Yeah.

01:09:17.125 --> 01:09:18.685
(laughing)

01:09:18.821 --> 01:09:20.061
What do you guys think?

01:09:20.196 --> 01:09:21.694
(overlapping chatter)

01:09:21.830 --> 01:09:23.032
-That was tight, bro.
-Yeah, that's it.

01:09:23.167 --> 01:09:24.497
MICHAEL:
Feels good?

01:09:24.633 --> 01:09:26.864
-(others chattering)
-All right.

01:09:28.371 --> 01:09:30.332
I want to try it
with music now.

01:09:30.467 --> 01:09:31.968
Yeah.

01:09:34.480 --> 01:09:37.607
In fact, I want to put you all
in my short film.

01:09:37.742 --> 01:09:39.109
-(chattering excitedly)
-Yo.

01:09:39.245 --> 01:09:40.280
Yeah!

01:09:40.416 --> 01:09:42.951
Let's crank it up, please.

01:09:43.086 --> 01:09:44.583
I want to feel it.

01:09:44.718 --> 01:09:46.855
MICHAEL:
♪ Beat it, beat it ♪

01:09:47.858 --> 01:09:50.890
♪ Showin' how funky
and strong is your fight ♪

01:09:51.026 --> 01:09:53.760
♪ It doesn't matter
who's wrong or right ♪

01:09:53.896 --> 01:09:56.125
-♪ Just beat it ♪
-♪ Beat it ♪

01:09:56.260 --> 01:09:58.134
-♪ Beat it ♪
-♪ Beat it ♪

01:09:58.269 --> 01:10:01.131
♪ No one wants to be defeated ♪

01:10:01.267 --> 01:10:04.871
♪ Showin' how funky
and strong is your fight ♪

01:10:05.007 --> 01:10:08.104
♪ It doesn't matter
who's wrong or right ♪

01:10:08.239 --> 01:10:11.175
♪ Just beat it, beat it,
beat it, beat it ♪

01:10:11.310 --> 01:10:13.415
-You know, CBS wants you
-♪ Beat it, beat it, beat it ♪

01:10:13.551 --> 01:10:14.784
