to tour with your brothers.

01:28:00.551 --> 01:28:03.078
Now, I let you do
that album by yourself.

01:28:04.148 --> 01:28:06.279
I'm gonna need you
to do this for me.

01:28:07.958 --> 01:28:09.524
For your family.

01:28:10.559 --> 01:28:12.652
I'm not a child anymore,
Joseph.

01:28:12.787 --> 01:28:14.254
(sighs heavily)

01:28:14.390 --> 01:28:15.660
-And you're not my manager.
-Here we go.

01:28:15.796 --> 01:28:17.994
I have to start
living my own life.

01:28:19.365 --> 01:28:21.162
On my own.

01:28:22.007 --> 01:28:23.733
Just like everyone else.

01:28:23.868 --> 01:28:25.804
You ain't like everyone else.

01:28:27.476 --> 01:28:29.169
So, you're trying to tell me

01:28:29.304 --> 01:28:31.678
you want to be treated
like an adult?

01:28:32.543 --> 01:28:33.977
All right.

01:28:34.112 --> 01:28:37.852
You want to
see what the world is like...

01:28:38.622 --> 01:28:41.253
...without a family
that protects you.

01:28:41.388 --> 01:28:42.815
(hinges creaking)

01:28:42.951 --> 01:28:45.058
Without a family that...

01:28:45.193 --> 01:28:46.762
understands you.

01:28:47.698 --> 01:28:50.864
Nobody else will understand you
outside this place.

01:28:50.999 --> 01:28:53.963
There you'll be with
all the money in the world,

01:28:54.098 --> 01:28:56.663
surrounded by people
who'll say "yes"

01:28:56.799 --> 01:28:59.200
to everything.

01:29:00.837 --> 01:29:03.204
Is that what you want?

01:29:06.449 --> 01:29:08.385
What kind of sense that make?

01:29:15.620 --> 01:29:17.926
I'm gonna...

01:29:18.062 --> 01:29:19.659
call Don King

01:29:19.795 --> 01:29:22.355
and tell him
you're doing the tour.

01:29:24.328 --> 01:29:27.030
I know you don't want
to let your family down.

01:29:29.669 --> 01:29:31.903
(Michael breathing deeply)

01:29:35.211 --> 01:29:37.073
(door closes)

01:29:38.180 --> 01:29:40.373
♪ ♪

01:29:45.923 --> 01:29:47.589
(sighs)

01:29:49.556 --> 01:29:50.817
(crowd cheering loudly)

01:29:50.953 --> 01:29:53.727
("Billie Jean" playing)

01:29:57.997 --> 01:30:00.227
♪ You're a whole
new generation ♪

01:30:00.363 --> 01:30:02.370
♪ You're lovin' what you do ♪

01:30:02.506 --> 01:30:04.397
♪ Put a Pepsi in the motion ♪

01:30:04.532 --> 01:30:06.370
♪ That choice is up to you,
hey-ey ♪

01:30:06.505 --> 01:30:08.369
-DIRECTOR: Cut! Cut! Cut! Cut!
-♪ You're the Pepsi... ♪

01:30:08.504 --> 01:30:10.276
-(music stops)
-MAN: We're cutting, guys.

01:30:11.112 --> 01:30:14.110
All right, here's what I need.
I'm thinking...

01:30:15.612 --> 01:30:17.614
...I'm gonna move the camera in
while you're up here.

01:30:18.117 --> 01:30:21.248
I need to get a close-up
of you at the top,

01:30:21.384 --> 01:30:23.083
so just feel the camera
as you come down.

01:30:23.218 --> 01:30:25.084
-Okay.
-Okay, great. All right.

01:30:25.220 --> 01:30:26.325
DIRECTOR:
Okay, everybody.

01:30:26.461 --> 01:30:27.761
(grunts) Here we go.

01:30:27.896 --> 01:30:30.665
What is this?
What do we got, take six?

01:30:30.800 --> 01:30:32.828
-(groans quietly)
-Lucky six. Lucky six.

01:30:32.964 --> 01:30:34.537
Here we go. Energy, everybody!

01:30:34.673 --> 01:30:37.173
You love the Jacksons.
You love the Jacksons.

01:30:37.309 --> 01:30:39.166
You love Pepsi. Let's go!

01:30:39.301 --> 01:30:41.673
-WOMAN: A marker!
-(marker snaps)

01:30:41.808 --> 01:30:43.104
-MAN 2: B mark!
-(marker snaps)

01:30:43.240 --> 01:30:44.842
-MAN 3: C mark.
-(audience cheering)

01:30:44.978 --> 01:30:46.807
-(marker snaps)
-DIRECTOR: And playback.

01:30:46.943 --> 01:30:50.344
("Billie Jean" playing)

01:30:53.114 --> 01:30:55.184
(fireworks explode)

01:31:04.600 --> 01:31:06.101
-(music fades)
-(sizzling)

01:31:06.236 --> 01:31:07.433
(muffled cheering)

01:31:07.568 --> 01:31:09.764
(distorted whimpering)

01:31:09.900 --> 01:31:12.300
(distorted moaning)

01:31:13.510 --> 01:31:14.942
-(music resumes)
-(screaming)

01:31:15.078 --> 01:31:16.303
Cut it.

01:31:16.439 --> 01:31:18.147
-MAN: Put it out!
-(Michael groaning)

01:31:18.282 --> 01:31:19.381
(microphone feedback)

01:31:19.516 --> 01:31:21.340
-(groaning)
-TITO: Michael!

01:31:21.476 --> 01:31:22.944
-(clamoring, screaming)
-(groaning)

01:31:23.080 --> 01:31:25.151
-What happened?
-(moaning)

01:31:25.286 --> 01:31:27.020
-BILL: Back up,
back up, back up.
-Bill, get him out of here.

01:31:27.156 --> 01:31:29.486
BILL: I'm here, I'm here,
I'm here, Michael.

01:31:29.621 --> 01:31:31.355
-Get him up, get him up.
-I'm here, Joker. I'm here.

01:31:31.490 --> 01:31:33.253
Hey, you're gonna
be okay, okay?
You're gonna be okay.

01:31:33.389 --> 01:31:34.759
BILL:
Come on, Mike. Clear a path!

01:31:34.894 --> 01:31:36.996
(people screaming
and clamoring)

01:31:37.999 --> 01:31:40.862
Out of my way!
Michael, I'm coming!

01:31:41.365 --> 01:31:42.999
-(moans)
-Get back! Get out of my way!

01:31:43.135 --> 01:31:45.542
Clear a path!
Get back! Get back!

01:31:46.743 --> 01:31:49.839
Clear a path!
Move! Move, please!

01:31:49.975 --> 01:31:52.544
(muffled shouting and wailing)

01:31:52.680 --> 01:31:54.683
BILL:
Excuse me!

01:31:55.548 --> 01:31:57.217
(whimpering)

01:31:57.352 --> 01:31:59.556
♪ ♪

01:32:06.955 --> 01:32:08.888
(phone ringing)

01:32:09.023 --> 01:32:10.523
(Joseph exhales)

01:32:11.633 --> 01:32:13.900
(continues tapping fingers)

01:32:17.409 --> 01:32:19.741
(indistinct P.A. announcement)

01:32:24.381 --> 01:32:26.506
Hey, Kate, come on.

01:32:28.452 --> 01:32:29.817
Hey, I need to talk to you.

01:32:29.952 --> 01:32:31.617
-Sir.
-I'm his father,
Joseph Jackson.

01:32:31.753 --> 01:32:33.482
This is his mother, Katherine.

01:32:33.617 --> 01:32:35.585
-Hi. It's good to meet you.
-Very nice to meet you.

01:32:35.720 --> 01:32:36.955
Thank you.

01:32:37.091 --> 01:32:38.626
Well, your son is
in stable condition.

01:32:38.762 --> 01:32:40.423
-All right.
-DOCTOR: All right?

01:32:40.559 --> 01:32:43.124
And, uh, we're trying to bring
his heart rate down,

01:32:43.259 --> 01:32:45.129
but he's in a lot of pain.

01:32:46.228 --> 01:32:47.600
Okay. When will he recover?

01:32:47.735 --> 01:32:49.132
It's too soon to tell.

01:32:49.268 --> 01:32:51.302
It's gonna be
a long road, all right?

01:32:51.438 --> 01:32:55.139
He has third-degree burns
and substantial nerve damage.

01:32:56.104 --> 01:32:57.938
JOSEPH:
Okay.

01:32:58.807 --> 01:33:01.742
Do you think he'll ever be
able to perform again?

01:33:01.877 --> 01:33:03.252
Ever?

01:33:03.387 --> 01:33:05.116
KATHERINE:
Joseph.

01:33:07.725 --> 01:33:11.390
Mr. Jackson,
your son almost died.

01:33:11.525 --> 01:33:12.925
I know that.

01:33:13.061 --> 01:33:14.821
Well, if that fire
had caught his clothes,

01:33:14.957 --> 01:33:17.759
or burned over to his face
and eyes, he wouldn't be here.

01:33:17.895 --> 01:33:19.460
I know my boy.

01:33:19.596 --> 01:33:21.768
And the only thing
that's gonna heal him

01:33:21.904 --> 01:33:23.497
is by getting
back on that stage.

01:33:24.805 --> 01:33:26.402
That's where he lives.

01:33:26.538 --> 01:33:28.141
-DOCTOR:
I understand that, sir.
-LA TOYA: Oh, my God.

01:33:28.276 --> 01:33:29.611
-But it's gonna be a while.
-Do you? All right.

01:33:29.747 --> 01:33:31.604
DOCTOR:
Yes, I do. But, Mr. Jackson...

01:33:31.739 --> 01:33:34.974
he's gonna need
your support to get there.

01:33:35.110 --> 01:33:36.851
I'm sorry.

01:33:39.113 --> 01:33:40.883
(exhales)

01:33:41.686 --> 01:33:43.188
WOMAN (shouting in distance):
Praying for you, Michael!

01:33:43.323 --> 01:33:45.119
DOCTOR: It's unlikely
that will grow back.

01:33:45.655 --> 01:33:48.896
You'll need surgery
to laser the scar tissue

01:33:49.031 --> 01:33:51.894
and stretch part of the scalp
over the burn.

01:33:52.697 --> 01:33:55.733
All right? We'll insert
an implant
to protect the scalp.

01:33:55.869 --> 01:33:57.867
Will I have to wear a wig?

01:33:58.003 --> 01:33:59.973
Well, right there on top.

01:34:02.010 --> 01:34:04.476
What kind of wig?
Like, a full wig?

01:34:04.611 --> 01:34:06.045
Hard to say.

01:34:06.180 --> 01:34:08.117
There are prosthetic
hair weaves we can try,

01:34:08.252 --> 01:34:11.512
but we won't know till we see
how the surgery goes next week.

01:34:14.020 --> 01:34:16.319
(indistinct P.A. announcement)

01:34:17.961 --> 01:34:19.492
(crowd shouting indistinctly
in the distance)

01:34:19.627 --> 01:34:21.227
You'll, um...

01:34:21.362 --> 01:34:23.829
you'll have to stay
on the Demerol for a while.

01:34:23.965 --> 01:34:25.799
I don't want
to take medication.

01:34:25.935 --> 01:34:27.831
I have to be honest,
Mr. Jackson,

01:34:27.967 --> 01:34:29.470
you're gonna need them.

01:34:30.040 --> 01:34:32.332
We have to replace
the implant periodically.

01:34:32.467 --> 01:34:34.444
The nerves
are exposed up there.

01:34:34.579 --> 01:34:36.570
You'll be in a lot of pain.

01:34:39.082 --> 01:34:42.081
I'll let you rest,
but I'll be back later.

01:34:47.522 --> 01:34:50.088
WOMAN: We'll stay here
till you're better, Michael!

01:34:50.224 --> 01:34:51.685
REPORTER:
You see the number of people

01:34:51.820 --> 01:34:53.924
who have already gathered
outside the hospital.

01:34:54.060 --> 01:34:55.291
If that isn't a testament

01:34:55.427 --> 01:34:57.025
to the star power
of Michael Jackson,

01:34:57.161 --> 01:34:58.793
I don't know what is.

01:34:58.928 --> 01:35:00.735
...say they won't go back
until Jackson is all right.

01:35:00.871 --> 01:35:02.904
-(donkey braying on TV)
-(door opens)

01:35:03.604 --> 01:35:05.032
All right.

01:35:05.167 --> 01:35:06.737
All right, Joker.

01:35:06.873 --> 01:35:08.370
Got all your favorites.

01:35:08.506 --> 01:35:09.878
-Golden Temple...
-(Katherine laughs)

01:35:10.013 --> 01:35:11.373
-they send their love.
-Golden Temple's

01:35:11.509 --> 01:35:12.580
-your favorite, Michael.
-Got some Mexican.

01:35:12.715 --> 01:35:14.113
Chinese. Some fried chicken.

01:35:14.248 --> 01:35:16.247
Even got these
little red candies you like.

01:35:17.355 --> 01:35:18.718
Thanks, Bill.

01:35:18.853 --> 01:35:20.850
You can just leave it there.

01:35:20.985 --> 01:35:22.550
I'm not hungry.

01:35:23.261 --> 01:35:25.421
Oh. Okay.

01:35:28.160 --> 01:35:29.730
I'll leave you all to it.

01:35:29.866 --> 01:35:32.868
-Okay. Thank you, Bill.
-Mm-hmm.

01:35:41.038 --> 01:35:43.179
(door closes)

01:35:43.314 --> 01:35:45.144
(monitor beeps)

01:36:00.257 --> 01:36:02.128
I'm sorry, Michael.

01:36:06.164 --> 01:36:08.466
I should have protected you.

01:36:09.469 --> 01:36:13.733
Mother, I don't want to
discuss this right now.

01:36:14.542 --> 01:36:16.109
Okay.

01:36:16.974 --> 01:36:18.848
(monitor beeps)

01:36:21.948 --> 01:36:24.117
No one can stop Joseph.

01:36:27.555 --> 01:36:29.155
Nobody.

01:36:37.133 --> 01:36:39.899
You just know that,
no matter what happens,

01:36:40.034 --> 01:36:42.696
I'm gonna be here for you...

01:36:43.506 --> 01:36:45.402
...always.

01:36:48.011 --> 01:36:50.077
I should get
some rest now, Mother.

01:37:02.052 --> 01:37:04.388
♪ ♪

01:37:14.166 --> 01:37:16.136
It's not your fault.

01:37:16.836 --> 01:37:19.139
♪ ♪

01:37:27.275 --> 01:37:29.248
(exhales)

01:37:33.381 --> 01:37:36.090
(breath trembling)

01:37:37.988 --> 01:37:41.260
WOMAN (in the distance):
The world needs you, Michael!

01:37:42.996 --> 01:37:44.692
(elevator bell dings)

01:37:54.170 --> 01:37:56.473
♪ ♪

01:38:15.998 --> 01:38:18.128
BRANCA:
How are you feeling?

01:38:18.264 --> 01:38:19.859
MICHAEL:
I'm okay.

01:38:19.994 --> 01:38:22.931
You know,
I'm still in a lot of pain.

01:38:23.767 --> 01:38:25.873
But the doctors say
I'm healing, so...

01:38:26.009 --> 01:38:27.636
BRANCA:
Well, that's good news.

01:38:28.404 --> 01:38:30.810
All these kids here...

01:38:30.946 --> 01:38:32.311
they won't fully heal

01:38:32.447 --> 01:38:35.315
and there's burns
all over their bodies.

01:38:35.851 --> 01:38:38.112
It just breaks my heart.

01:38:38.248 --> 01:38:40.121
It truly does.

01:38:41.583 --> 01:38:43.916
You know, it got me thinking...

01:38:45.422 --> 01:38:47.329
I need to do more for them.

01:38:48.132 --> 01:38:50.129
How much are we getting
for the accident?

01:38:50.265 --> 01:38:52.827
It should be
around seven figures.

01:38:52.962 --> 01:38:56.138
I need every penny donated
to the burn center here.

01:38:57.074 --> 01:38:59.199
Please, you got to
make that happen.

01:38:59.334 --> 01:39:00.669
Yeah, of course.

01:39:01.512 --> 01:39:03.470
(Michael sighs)

01:39:03.606 --> 01:39:06.147
I'm getting really sleepy.

01:39:07.584 --> 01:39:09.480
These pain meds.

01:39:12.249 --> 01:39:13.616
You get some rest

01:39:13.751 --> 01:39:15.486
and I'll come
check on you tomorrow.

01:39:16.152 --> 01:39:17.917
Okay.

01:39:19.096 --> 01:39:21.491
-Did you bring that?
-Oh, the mouse.

01:39:21.627 --> 01:39:24.495
-Yeah. That's from me.
-(chuckles)

01:39:25.429 --> 01:39:27.267
-I love that.
-Good.

01:39:27.902 --> 01:39:29.135
Thank you, Branca.

01:39:29.271 --> 01:39:31.172
-I'll see you tomorrow.
-See you.

01:39:32.409 --> 01:39:34.703
JOSEPH: If that boy doesn't
 go on tour...

01:39:35.805 --> 01:39:38.313
...everything we have
falls apart.

01:39:38.448 --> 01:39:41.873
I'm talking deals,
sponsorships, our reputation.

01:39:42.009 --> 01:39:43.782
Everything.
Everything just gone.

01:39:43.917 --> 01:39:45.153
Everything here.

01:39:46.223 --> 01:39:48.920
The boys won't be able
to tour anymore.

01:39:49.056 --> 01:39:50.418
Not without Michael.

01:39:50.554 --> 01:39:53.986
Your son just got out of ICU.

01:39:56.500 --> 01:39:59.025
Michael never wanted to do
the Victory tour to begin with.

01:39:59.160 --> 01:40:03.039
You planned this entire thing
behind his back.

01:40:06.169 --> 01:40:07.769
(sighs)

01:40:13.813 --> 01:40:16.976
When are you gonna realize
he's on his own path?

01:40:19.652 --> 01:40:22.421
And sometimes, you need
to get out of the way.

01:40:25.393 --> 01:40:27.987
Otherwise,
you're gonna lose him.

01:40:31.033 --> 01:40:33.099
What about the other boys?

01:40:33.234 --> 01:40:35.830
They'll find their own path.

01:40:51.045 --> 01:40:52.954
MICHAEL:
 You know something, Bill?

01:40:53.089 --> 01:40:54.387
BILL:
What's that?

01:40:54.522 --> 01:40:56.152
MICHAEL:
God's been very good to me.

01:40:56.288 --> 01:40:58.424
That he has. (chuckles)

01:40:59.225 --> 01:41:00.763
Not just the accident.

01:41:00.898 --> 01:41:04.232
You know, I... I almost died...

01:41:05.531 --> 01:41:07.664
...but I was given
a second chance.

01:41:08.530 --> 01:41:10.497
Yeah, well...

01:41:10.633 --> 01:41:12.471
God gave you a gift, son.

01:41:13.601 --> 01:41:15.309
A platform...

01:41:16.045 --> 01:41:17.806
...to reach the whole world.

01:41:19.576 --> 01:41:21.282
I can't ignore that.

01:41:22.685 --> 01:41:24.978
No.

01:41:27.749 --> 01:41:29.790
I have to shine my light.

01:41:29.926 --> 01:41:32.986
Spread love and joy.

01:41:34.092 --> 01:41:35.890
To heal.

01:41:40.637 --> 01:41:42.270
Yeah.

01:41:44.733 --> 01:41:46.406
That's my destiny.

01:41:48.373 --> 01:41:50.303
I truly believe that.

01:41:50.438 --> 01:41:53.138
Well, why don't we focus
on getting you healthy first,

01:41:53.273 --> 01:41:54.948
then we can do all those
things you need to do.

01:41:55.084 --> 01:41:56.845
I'm gonna do the tour.

01:41:57.678 --> 01:41:59.016
Are you sure?

01:41:59.152 --> 01:42:01.388
For my family.

01:42:02.620 --> 01:42:04.985
But then I'm ready, Bill.

01:42:09.025 --> 01:42:11.831
I'm gonna look him
straight in the eye.

01:42:11.966 --> 01:42:14.335
This is my life.

01:42:16.772 --> 01:42:18.504
My path.

01:42:22.811 --> 01:42:24.312
Mine.

01:42:26.442 --> 01:42:29.178
♪ ♪

01:42:29.313 --> 01:42:31.682
(crowd cheering)

01:42:37.926 --> 01:42:40.889
♪ ♪

01:42:46.034 --> 01:42:47.967
MICHAEL: Okay, let's go out
 there and tear that stage up.

01:42:48.102 --> 01:42:49.702
MARLON:
 Yeah.

01:42:49.837 --> 01:42:51.029
MICHAEL: Give the audience
 what they deserve.

01:42:51.165 --> 01:42:52.439
-TITO: Yeah.
-The best show ever.

01:42:53.541 --> 01:42:55.541
JOSEPH:
 I told you what to think.

01:42:56.406 --> 01:42:58.038
I love you guys.

01:42:58.173 --> 01:42:59.711
JOSEPH:
 You ain't like everyone else.

01:42:59.846 --> 01:43:01.347
 You think you're better
 than me, boy?

01:43:01.482 --> 01:43:02.745
TITO:
 Love you, too, Mike.

01:43:02.880 --> 01:43:04.450
-I really do.
-Love you, too, Mike.

01:43:04.585 --> 01:43:06.415
JOSEPH:
 Nobody else will understand you

01:43:06.551 --> 01:43:09.089
 outside this place.

01:43:09.224 --> 01:43:10.891
"The Jacksons" on three. One...

01:43:11.026 --> 01:43:12.795
 two, three...

01:43:12.930 --> 01:43:14.263
ALL:
Jacksons!

01:43:15.695 --> 01:43:17.563
JOSEPH:
 After I give these boys a rest,

01:43:17.698 --> 01:43:19.265
 I'm planning
 an international tour.

01:43:19.401 --> 01:43:20.863
REPORTER:
 With Michael?

01:43:20.999 --> 01:43:23.199
Yeah, we're gonna hit
all the big arenas

01:43:23.335 --> 01:43:24.598
and stadiums.

01:43:24.734 --> 01:43:26.331
This is just the beginning

01:43:26.467 --> 01:43:27.904
 -of the Victory tour.
 -You adding more shows?

01:43:28.039 --> 01:43:30.611
(chuckles): Yeah,
we gonna hit every continent.

01:43:30.747 --> 01:43:33.843
But, first of all, we're going
to Paris, London, Tokyo,

01:43:33.979 --> 01:43:36.347
South Africa. You name it,
we gonna be there.

01:43:36.482 --> 01:43:37.710
